<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Computer Hub</title>

<style>
*{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    box-sizing:border-box;
    font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
}

body{
    background:#f4f4f4;
    color:#333;
}

header{
    background:#ffffff;
    padding:20px 10%;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
    align-items:center;
    border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;
}

header h1{
    font-size:28px;
}

nav a{
    text-decoration:none;
    color:#333;
    margin-left:20px;
    font-weight:bold;
}

nav a:hover{
    color:#0078ff;
}

.hero{
    text-align:center;
    padding:80px 20px;
}

.hero h2{
    font-size:42px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.hero p{
    font-size:18px;
    color:#666;
    max-width:700px;
    margin:auto;
}

.button{
    display:inline-block;
    margin-top:30px;
    padding:12px 25px;
    background:#0078ff;
    color:white;
    text-decoration:none;
    border-radius:5px;
}

.button:hover{
    background:#005fcc;
}

section{
    padding:60px 10%;
    background:white;
    margin-top:20px;
}

section h2{
    text-align:center;
    margin-bottom:20px;
}

.cards{
    display:flex;
    gap:20px;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    justify-content:center;
}

.card{
    width:280px;
    background:#fafafa;
    border:1px solid #ddd;
    border-radius:10px;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
    transition:.3s;
}

.card:hover{
    transform:translateY(-5px);
}

.card h3{
    margin-bottom:10px;
}

footer{
    background:#222;
    color:white;
    text-align:center;
    padding:20px;
    margin-top:20px;
}

@media(max-width:768px){

header{
    flex-direction:column;
}

nav{
    margin-top:10px;
}

.hero h2{
    font-size:30px;
}

.cards{
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
}

}
</style>

</head>
<body>

<header>
    <h1>Computer Hub</h1>

    <nav>
        <a href="#">Home</a>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
        <a href="#components">Components</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
</header>

<section class="hero">
    <h2>Welcome to Computer Hub</h2>

    <p>
        Computers make our daily lives easier by helping us study, work,
        communicate, and create amazing things. Learn the basics of computer
        hardware and technology on this simple website.
    </p>

    <a href="#components" class="button">Explore</a>
</section>

<section id="about">
    <h2>About Computers</h2>

    <p style="text-align:center; max-width:800px; margin:auto;">
        A computer is an electronic device that accepts data, processes it,
        stores information, and produces useful results. Computers are used in
        schools, businesses, hospitals, and homes around the world.
    </p>
</section>

<section id="components">

<h2>Main Computer Components</h2>

<div class="cards">

<div class="card">
<h3>CPU</h3>
<p>
The Central Processing Unit (CPU) is known as the brain of the computer because
it performs calculations and executes instructions.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>RAM</h3>
<p>
Random Access Memory (RAM) temporarily stores information while programs are
running, making the computer faster.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Storage</h3>
<p>
Storage devices such as SSDs and HDDs permanently save files, documents,
photos, and applications.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>GPU</h3>
<p>
The Graphics Processing Unit (GPU) creates images, videos, and improves gaming
performance.
</p>
</div>

</div>

</section>

<section id="contact">

<h2>Project Information</h2>

<p style="text-align:center;">
This website was created as a simple HTML and CSS project for educational
purposes.
</p>

<br>

<p style="text-align:center;">
<strong>Created by:</strong><br>
Jorge Denmark Garcia
</p>

</section>

<footer>
    © 2026 Computer Hub <br><br>
    Website Created by <strong>Jorge Denmark Garcia</strong>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
